### REST Client — S6.3 OAuth2 / OpenID Connect. API local.
### Todo es lógica pura (flujos, PKCE, authorize URL): offline.

@host = http://localhost:5090

### Health
GET {{host}}/health

### Flujo recomendado por tipo de cliente (slide 5)
GET {{host}}/oauth/flujo?cliente=Spa
###
GET {{host}}/oauth/flujo?cliente=DaemonOServicio
###
GET {{host}}/oauth/flujo?cliente=Cli

### ¿Flujo deprecado? (slide 5)
GET {{host}}/oauth/deprecado/Implicit
###
GET {{host}}/oauth/deprecado/AuthorizationCodePkce

### Generar par PKCE (slide 6)
GET {{host}}/oauth/pkce

### Plan de login completo (flujo + authorize URL + PKCE, slide 5-6)
POST {{host}}/oauth/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cliente": "Spa",
  "tenantId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "clientId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "redirectUri": "http://localhost:5173/callback",
  "scopes": ["openid", "profile", "api://api-ventas/Pedidos.Read"]
}

### Plan para un daemon (Client Credentials, sin authorize URL)
POST {{host}}/oauth/plan
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "cliente": "DaemonOServicio",
  "tenantId": "11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111",
  "clientId": "22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222",
  "redirectUri": "",
  "scopes": ["api://api-ventas/.default"]
}
